# .gitleaksignore — stop-words for gitleaks scan (see .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml).
#
# Format: one entry per line. Each entry is matched as an EXACT substring
# against a finding's fingerprint of the form `<file>:<ruleID>:<startLine>`
# (the same `<commit-hash>:<file>:<ruleID>:<line>` form printed by
# `gitleaks detect --verbose`). Wildcards / regex / pure file-path entries
# are NOT supported by gitleaks v8.18.x — to suppress a finding you must
# spell out the precise file + rule + line triple.
#
# Only entries below are intentional.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LPR-002 / DR-001 — historical Resend live-key leak in root test-*.js scripts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Five root-level scratch scripts (test-contact.js, test-direct.js,
# test-key-check.js, test-keys.js, test-resend.js) hardcoded a live Resend
# API key (prefix `re_`, see LPR-002 / Resend dashboard for the exact value)
# in git history from their introduction (commit 16c962b) through commit
# f181cec (parent of b11f9f5), which scrubbed them to a
# `REDACTED_USE_RESEND_API_KEY_ENV` placeholder.
# The placeholder commit did NOT rewrite history, so the original key is
# still in the object store and every clone/fork/cached checkout.
#
# This allowlist exists ONLY so the scanner can keep detecting NEW leaks
# rather than failing forever on historical ones that have already been
# triaged and are owned under LPR-002.
#
# The exposed key MUST still be rotated at the Resend dashboard. Removing
# these allowlist lines after history is purged (git filter-repo + coordinated
# force-push) is part of closing LPR-002 — not optional.
#
# Only the two of the five files that ALSO tripped gitleaks' generic-api-key
# rule (key/api-key variables assigned in the working file) are listed below.
# The remaining three matched only as constructor-arg contexts and were not
# flagged — separate coverage gap, tracked separately.
test-direct.js:generic-api-key:2
test-key-check.js:generic-api-key:3
